moveit2: shared_ptr::use_count() == 1 for shared_ptr::unique()

std::shared_ptr::unique() was deprecated in C++17 and removed in C++20;
QNX's libc++ drops it in C++20 mode, which some of these targets build with
(kinematics_plugin_loader.cpp: "'kinematics::KinematicsBasePtr' has no member
named 'unique'"); elsewhere it warns. use_count() == 1 is what unique()
returned. (qnx-ports/aports' moveit2.patch makes the same change.)

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
diff --git a/moveit_core/collision_detection/src/world.cpp b/moveit_core/collision_detection/src/world.cpp
index b2262f9..2886e38 100644
--- a/moveit_core/collision_detection/src/world.cpp
+++ b/moveit_core/collision_detection/src/world.cpp
@@ -130,7 +130,7 @@ World::ObjectConstPtr World::getObject(const std::string& object_id) const
 
 void World::ensureUnique(ObjectPtr& obj)
 {
-  if (obj && !obj.unique())
+  if (obj && !(obj.use_count() == 1))
     obj = std::make_shared<Object>(*obj);
 }
 
